# The manuscript is deliberately not in this repository.
manuscripts/
# Square brackets are glob metacharacters in gitignore -- an unescaped
# [READY] would be read as the character class R,E,A,D,Y and match nothing
# here. The trailing space in the real directory name is also significant,
# so match on the stable tail instead of reproducing the name exactly.
\[READY\]*
*P11 /
*(S&P*)*
tenantsafe_draft.pdf
*.pdf

# Coordinated-disclosure material. Held out on purpose: the Home Assistant
# finding is UNDISCLOSED, and git history survives a later visibility change,
# so committing this now would publish it if the repo is ever made public --
# even if the file were deleted first.
disclosure/

# Generated. `./build_artifact.sh` reassembles artifact/ from the sources here.
artifact/
results/*.tar.gz

# Agent workspace: contains a nested git worktree, which cannot be committed
# into an outer repository and would not clone correctly.
.claude/

# Local noise
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.rka/
cfg-*/

# Live credentials. The SmartThings personal access token grants control of a
# real account; git history survives a visibility change, so this must never be
# committed even once.
.env
.env.*
*.pat
smartthings-token*

# Manuscript-bearing archives. prepare_upload.sh writes its bundle to the
# parent of the manuscript directory, which after the 2026-09-17 move is the
# repository root rather than the ignored manuscripts/ tree, so the upload ZIP
# now lands here. Both of these carry main.tex, refs.bib and sections/.
*.zip
